    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_body">Author: 念.\nEmail: 3471348199@qq.com,\n
        xujiekai508@gmail.com\nOriginal project author: The Android Open Source Project
        (AOSP)\n\nProject overview:\nThis project migrates and maintains classic Android live
        wallpapers. The goal is to fully preserve original visuals while modernizing the rendering
        stack for compatibility, performance, and stability on current Android versions.\n\nCore
        goals:\n1) Visual fidelity: faithfully reproduce leaf drift, water ripples, colors, and
        timing.\n2) Performance and stability: reduce CPU/GPU load and improve high-refresh
        smoothness.\n3) Long-term compatibility: work on Android 10+ and keep a future migration
        path.\n\nWhy migrate from RenderScript to OpenGL ES 2.0:\n- RenderScript is deprecated and
        removed from recent SDK/NDK toolchains.\n- It is fragile across devices and ROMs with
        frequent rendering failures.\n- OpenGL ES 2.0 is widely supported and enables GPU-based
        optimization.</string>

